body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:e71ba9245540ab1bc20c8be835cb343846df32ce576ad5fa6e39c2f21f20cc5d","file":"preprints/Exponential-decay-in-two-dimensional-classical-On-models-September-23-2026/build/main.tex","line":89,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"9f1007e2bb5bf8a9a90c4e90c81104063ea7749c1048ba11b47451fdb092f812","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Exponential-decay-in-two-dimensional-classical-On-models-September-23-2026/build/main.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:e71ba9245540ab1bc20c8be835cb343846df32ce576ad5fa6e39c2f21f20cc5d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Exponential-decay-in-two-dimensional-classical-On-models-September-23-2026/build/main.tex#L89"},"statement_kind":"corollary","text":"\\label{cor:limits}\nLet $\\Lambda_L=[-L,L]^2\\cap\\Z^2$, with all its nearest-neighbor edges,\nfree boundary conditions, and constant strength $\\beta>0$. For every\n$n\\ge3$ and $x\\in\\Z^2$,\n\\begin{equation}\n \\limsup_{L\\to\\infty}\n \\left|\\langle\\sigma_0\\cdot\\sigma_x\\rangle_{\\Lambda_L,\\beta}^{(n)}\\right|\n \\le A e^{-m\\|x\\|_2},\n \\label{eq:limsup}\n\\end{equation}\nwith the constants of Theorem~\\ref{thm:main}. Every subsequential local\nweak limit of these laws satisfies the same two-point bound."}
